{"summary":"Reject the amendment. Existing tests already cover the added non-critical-GH summary path, and the cited regression risk is not demonstrated beyond that.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-77b8e070","decision":"reject","rationale":"The code change does add a new \"score\" detail on the non-critical-GH path, but that behavior is already exercised by the existing molt-failure test that asserts the summary contains \"score\". The newer disabled-GH-minimum test is specifically checking branch selection by ensuring the critical-GH detail is suppressed. Because the else branch is unconditional for all non-critical-GH failures, requiring an additional positive assertion in that exact scenario would be redundant rather than addressing a distinct correctness or safety gap, and there is no evidence here of consumers depending on exact summary strings as a stable interface."}]}